                <pb facs="0444" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 S/217: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-16T15:00:00-05:00">January 16, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Your 42, January 13, 3 p.m. Department concurs in your views expressed in
                    paragraph 2. Legation should insist upon observance of procedure laid down in
                    Article 3 of Shanghai Land Regulations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
